 County runs 75 years back to 1951, and on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 6 grids June to July came in under 90% of normal in 40 of them, more than any other pair. In 2025 the middle of the grids got 60% of normal in February to March and 57% in October to November. So far in 2026 it got 141% in March to April. Every grid had its driest year in 1988, with grid 24749 at 53%.</p>"}
